# ek-widgetdrop: OPERATE the course editor -- move the cursor onto the CREATE
# top-bar item, press A to drop its menu open, then B to close it.
#
# EXPANSION-KIT-ONLY AND DISK-ONLY, exactly as ek-courseedit.gdxs explains:
# main_menu.c:222's EK arm bounces the cursor off MODE_COURSE_EDIT (4) whenever
# gLeoDriveConnectionState == 0. NOT a corpus replay, SHOTs hand-placed -- what is
# being proved is that a specific widget state exists and what it looks like.
#
# B11o. ektranslate's biggest stated gap was "nothing was OPERATED in either
# editor": both prior EK replays enter a screen and sit there. This one opens a
# drop-down, which is the only way to reach func_xk1_800276B0's narrow-scissor arm
# (expansion_kit/A3AE0.c:1033).
#
# Derivation of every number below, from the decomp's own data:
#  - cursor starts at (160, 120)          course_edit/188850.c:47
#  - stick step is 0.05*stick/2 px/tick   course_edit/188850.c:1009
#    so stickX=-80 is -2 px/tick and stickY=+80 is -2 px/tick
#  - 56 ticks left  : x 160 -> 48
#  - 46 ticks up    : y 120 -> 28
#  - CREATE is gCourseEditWidget item 0, hit box x [24,72) y [20,36)
#    (A3AE0.c:759 left=24 top=20 xStep=48, hit test A3AE0.c:816)
#    so (48, 28) is the centre of item 0 in both axes.
#  - A there opens gCreateWidget (left=24, top=36, 6 items, yStep=16).
#  - B closes it (A3AE0.c func_xk1_80027B74, via 19DD60.c:275).
build native/ekwidget
seed1 0x1234abcd
seed2 0x0fedcba9
pins renderthread=1 bridgemain=1 det=1
note CREATE drop-down: gCreateWidget left=24 top=36 yStep=16, 6 items 48x16.
at 350
wait 1
at 400
press START 15 0
at 600
wait 1
shot menu_before
at 660
press DOWN 12 0
at 760
wait 1
shot menu_cursor
at 820
press A 12 0
at 1100
wait 1
shot editor
at 1200
stick -80 0 56
at 1300
stick 0 80 46
at 1400
wait 1
shot cursor_create
at 1440
press A 12 0
at 1560
wait 1
shot drop_open_0
at 1800
wait 1
shot drop_open_1
at 2100
wait 1
shot drop_open_2
at 2300
press B 12 0
at 2450
wait 1
shot drop_closed_0
at 2700
wait 1
shot drop_closed_1
len 2900
